      "text": "Software supply chain campaign and its unnamed operator, first reported by GitGuardian in September 2025: malicious GitHub Actions workflows named \"Github Actions Security\" injected into compromised repositories exfiltrated CI/CD secrets, with 3,325 secrets stolen from 817 repositories. In October 2026 OpenSourceMalware reported a renewed wave and a second stage that no longer needs a CI runner: a .vscode/tasks.json launcher with a folderOpen trigger runs a Node.js credential stealer disguised as public/fonts/fa-solid-400.woff2, installs a cron job polling the operator's server, and is backed by a fallback workflow. OpenSourceMalware calls this stage a copycat of the DPRK PolinRider..."
